TITLE:: Pconstraint
SUMMARY:: Bounded depth-first search for complete finite sequences
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events>Patterns>Patternarium
RELATED:: Classes/Pscan, Classes/PgraphWalk, Classes/Pseed

DESCRIPTION::
Solves each complete finite sequence before yielding any of it. Constraints receive a fresh shallow history Array, candidate, zero-based position and latest inval, and must return a Boolean. A Function or Collection of Functions is accepted; an empty collection imposes no restrictions. This is a sequential finite solver, not a complete general-purpose CSP engine.

Depth-first search enumerates candidates in their supplied order, optionally shuffling copied domains with the thread RNG. Function domains are re-evaluated on each entry into a position and may depend on that prefix. Pattern domains are sampled once per position at stream start, then cached for backtracking; early exhaustion is an Error. Literal domains are reused. Nil candidates are invalid, and duplicate candidates can produce repeated solutions.

Length is at most 4096, each candidate collection at most 100000. A rejected candidate or exhausted search position consumes one backtrack unit. Exceeding maxBacktracks always throws a distinct budget Error, regardless of failure mode, even after earlier complete solutions were emitted. Failure mode applies only to a naturally exhausted search with no solutions. If fewer than requested solutions exist, any complete solutions already emitted are retained and the stream ends. Zero length has exactly one empty solution; values mode yields nothing for it. Solutions zero consumes no domains.

Yielded solution Arrays are fresh shallow copies. Values mode yields each solution's items directly. State is stream-local, but callbacks and contained candidate objects can still reference caller state. Memory depends on cached position domains and active candidate lists, with exponential worst-case search work bounded by the failure budget and requested solution count. Iterative search avoids recursive call-stack growth.

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: domain
Finite Collection reused at each position; Function(index, history, inval) returning a finite Collection; or Pattern yielding one finite Collection per position.
ARGUMENT:: constraints
Function or literal collection of Functions taking history, candidate, index, inval.
ARGUMENT:: length
Required finite nonnegative Integer, sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: solutions
Finite nonnegative Integer, default 1; sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: randomize
Boolean, default false; sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: maxBacktracks
Nonnegative Integer, default 10000; sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: failure
empty (default), warn or error; sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: output
solution (default) or values; sampled once. Once-sampled arguments accept literals, Functions or Patterns.

INSTANCEMETHODS::
METHOD:: storeArgs
Returns constructor arguments in public constructor order.
METHOD:: embedInStream
Runs the stream, yielding values and returning the latest inval at termination.

EXAMPLES::
code::
Pconstraint([0, 1, 2], { |h, x| h.includes(x).not }, 3, 2).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pconstraint / Value stream
var values = {
Pconstraint([0, 1, 2], { |h, x| h.includes(x).not }, 3, 2).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
values = values.flatten(1);
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: x, dur: 0.2, amp: 0.08)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Musical example
Load the example instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments:: first.
code::
(
Pbind(\instrument, \fmPiano,
    \degree, Pconstraint((0..7), { |h, x| h.isEmpty or: { (x - h.last).abs <= 2 } }, 16, output: \values),
    \dur, 0.125).play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Voice leading with bounded leaps
code::
Pconstraint([0, 2, 4, 5], { |h, x| h.isEmpty or: { (x-h.last).abs <= 2 } }, 6).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pconstraint / Voice leading with bounded leaps
var values = {
Pconstraint([0, 2, 4, 5], { |h, x| h.isEmpty or: { (x-h.last).abs <= 2 } }, 6).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
values = values.flatten(1);
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: x, dur: 0.2, amp: 0.08)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Simple counterpoint-like restrictions
code::
Pconstraint({ |i| [4, 5, 7] + [0, 2, 4, 2][i] },
    { |h, x, i| [3, 4, 7].includes((x - [0, 2, 4, 2][i]) % 12) }, 4).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pconstraint / Simple counterpoint-like restrictions
var values = {
Pconstraint({ |i| [4, 5, 7] + [0, 2, 4, 2][i] },
    { |h, x, i| [3, 4, 7].includes((x - [0, 2, 4, 2][i]) % 12) }, 4).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
values = values.flatten(1);
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: x, dur: 0.2, amp: 0.08)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: All-interval row in a small space
code::
Pconstraint((0..3), { |h, x|
    h.includes(x).not and: {
        h.isEmpty or: { h.differentiate.drop(1).abs.includes((x-h.last).abs).not }
    }
}, 4).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
